  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 407 AM EDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\n- A few showers are possible today\n\nFeel most areas will remain dry today, but it is not out of the\nrealm of possibilities to see a few light showers today. Current\nregional radar loops confirm a showers continue across the area \ndespite the deeper convection pushing south an hour or two ago. \nThe showers will be associated with weak shortwave dropping south\nthrough the northern flow aloft. Residual moisture hangs on into\nat least the midday hours before drier air sweeps in this\nafternoon and evening. Only have 20-30 pct chances for a shower\nmainly this morning.\n\n- High confidence in dry weather this afternoon through Tuesday\n\nBUFKIT overviews and ensemble members of the GFS and ECMWF confirm\nthat there is very little chance for precipitation in our area\nfrom this evening through Tuesday. For those that have received\nheavy rain in the last 3-5 days it will give those areas a chance\nto dry out.\n\n- Temperatures to be fairly close to normals through the period\n\nTemperatures will be close to normal for this time of year through\nthe 7 day forecast period (Normals for today: highs in the upper \n70s / lows in the upper 50s). We will see highs push into the 80s\nonce again early next week in the southerly flow ahead of a mid\nweek cold front.",
